{
  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, PCA) achieves 0.485 accuracy while config_010 (image-only, ResNet50) achieves only 0.208, a large gap that creates critical uncertainty about whether the image modality is fundamentally uninformative for this task or whether ResNet50 is simply a poor encoder. Question: config_013 (image-only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) is a clean single-variable change from config_010, isolating the effect of the image encoder. If ViT-L substantially improves over ResNet50, it validates the image modality and justifies investing in multimodal fusion configs (016-051). If it also performs poorly, we can eliminate the majority of multimodal configurations from consideration and redirect budget toward RNA encoder improvements (scvi, scgpt) and profile/aggregation settings. Why best next experiment: With only 2 data points, the most consequential uncertainty is whether the image modality can contribute at all. Resolving this gates decisions on ~36 multimodal configs and determines whether to focus remaining budget on RNA improvements or multimodal fusion, making it the highest-information-value single experiment under a limited budget."
}

